\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  410\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  -425\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\b\fs24\chcbpat17 Ps.-M\u257 \'e2\u353 \'f0\u257 \'e2\u702 ?all\u257 \'e2h Ibn-A\u7791 ?ar\u299 \'ee}}\plain \f2\b\fs24  (Messahalla):\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 De compositione astrolabi (Translatio Johannis Hispalensis)}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  
\par \pard\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Prohemium in astrolabium Messehallach 1445\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .< {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Scito quod astrolabium est nomen grecum}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \endash ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  est comparacio stature tue ad planiciem etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   >{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5686/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 1\u183 \'b74\u183 \'b75\u183 \'b70\u183 \'b7}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  < >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Explicit astrolabium Mesahalla\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  <; 425\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   leer. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  
\par \pard\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 Edition: Robert T. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Gunther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Chaucer and Messahalla on the astrolabe. Now printed in full for the first time with the original illustrations. Oxford 1929 (Early science in Oxford 5), S. 195-216. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Thorndike/Kibre\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Sp. 1409. \endash  Gegen Messahalla als Verfasser und zur Entstehung des Textes als Kompilation des 13. Jh.s auf Basis verschiedener Quellen vgl. Paul \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kunitzsch\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , On the authenticity of the treatise on the composition and use of the astrolabe ascribed to Messahalla, in: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ders.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , The Arabs and the stars. Texts and traditions on the fixed stars, and their influence in medieval Europe. Northampton 1989, Nr. X (Wiederabdruck aus: Archives internationales d\rquote historie des sciences 31 (1986), S. 42-62). \endash  Vgl. ferner \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Gerl\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Astronom (wie oben), S. 56.}

